      <div class="seg heap-elastic" style="width:73.2%;">M</div>
      <div class="seg nonheap" style="width:7.8%;">B</div>
      <div class="seg headroom" style="width:19%;">K</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="row-label">After GC (conditions permitting)</div>
    <div class="bar-container">
      <div class="seg heap-elastic" style="width:39%;">N</div>
      <div class="seg nonheap" style="width:7.8%;">B</div>
      <div class="seg headroom" style="width:53.2%;">O</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="key">
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#6fa3cc;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>E — Heap committed (Xms)</strong> <span class="qty">(~3000 MiB — smaller starting commitment)</span></div></div>
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#d99a3c;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>B — Non-heap</strong> <span class="qty">(~800 MiB)</span></div></div>
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#fff; border-color:#999;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>L — Unclaimed</strong> <span class="qty">(~6440 MiB — available for heap to grow into)</span></div></div>
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#6fa3cc;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>M — Heap grown to Xmx</strong> <span class="qty">(~7500 MiB — comfortably above observed ~6.6 GiB peak)</span></div></div>
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#fff; border-color:#999;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>K — Headroom at peak</strong> <span class="qty">(~1940 MiB)</span></div></div>
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#6fa3cc;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>N — Heap, can shrink</strong> <span class="qty">(~4000 MiB — if post-GC occupancy drops far enough)</span></div></div>
    <div class="key-item"><span class="key-swatch" style="background:#fff; border-color:#999;"></span><div class="key-text"><strong>O — Reclaimed headroom</strong> <span class="qty">(~5440 MiB — best-case; not guaranteed under real-world load)</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout good">
    <code>-Xms3g -Xmx7500m</code> + container 10Gi. ~1.9 GiB headroom even at sustained peak (Proposal 2's
    reliable win), <em>and</em> lower startup/low-load RSS floor (Proposal 1's contribution). OS reclaim after
    GC is a bonus if conditions allow, not a guarantee. This is the recommended combination.
  </div>
